  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A Slot wider than its tool now runs one wall lap at each level, after the rows.\n- The lap follows the boundary of the tool centre stadium: two straight sides and two half circles.\n- Each half circle is a chain of arcs (G02/G03). The chain is split at every row end on it and at its tip, so no arc is more than 90 degrees.\n- The rows and the lap compute a row end with one function (`cap_point`). Each row join meets the lap at the same point to the bit.\n- The lap starts where the last row ends and closes at that point.\n- Under `climb` the lap is counterclockwise (the slot's air on the left, the same sense as the rows). Under conventional it is clockwise.\n- A full-width slot (`h = 0`, one row on the centre line) does not change.\n- The lap code is in the new module `crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot_lap.rs`. `slots.rs` is 394 lines.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2906-slot-round-ends.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nA row touches a round end only at its end point. The move between two rows is a straight line. The tool did not follow the arc between two row ends. On a 10 mm slot with a 6 mm tool, 0.86 mm stayed on the wall of each round end.\n\n## Why the arcs are split at the row ends\n\nThe first version used two quarter arcs for each cap. The quick gate refused it on 8 app suites. The verifier's crossing law (a) flattens an arc into chords inside its circle. A row join is a chord that ends exactly on the circle, so it crossed those flattened chords, and the post was held. With the split, the join and the lap share their vertices. The law reads a shared vertex as a touch, not a crossing. The crossing law does not change.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New pin: `crates/motion/tests/slot_round_ends.rs`\n  - `wide_slot_cuts_its_round_ends_climb`\n  - `wide_slot_cuts_its_round_ends_conventional`\n  - `wide_slot_with_rows_off_the_tips_cuts_its_round_ends`\n  - Each point on the stadium wall must be within the tool radius of the tool centre path (limit 0.01 mm). No tool centre point may leave the cutter centre stadium. `crossed_pairs` (the verifier's crossing law) must be empty.\n  - Red before the fix: `climb=true z=9: 0.855 mm left on the wall at (28.536, 18.536)`.\n- New unit tests in `slot_lap.rs`: the lap closes on its start; each row end is a lap vertex; CCW from `b` runs the +n side first; CW from `b` turns round `b` first.\n- Mutations:\n  - `slots.rs` set back to `upstream/main`: the pin fails (0.855 mm, both directions). Restored: green.\n  - The cap split without the row ends (tangent points and tip only): `wide_slot_with_rows_off_the_tips_cuts_its_round_ends` fails with 22 crossing pairs. Restored: green.\n- Expected-change test updates:\n  - `crates/motion/tests/machining2d.rs`: `slot_offsets_rows_across_a_wide_channel`, `conventional_slot_starts_at_the_far_end`, `slot_stock_to_leave_narrows_the_center_area` read the rows as the prefix of the level and pin the lap (arc count, direction, tips at x = -7 and 47, close at the last row end). `slot_helix_orbits_in_the_certified_channel` counts only descending arcs as the helix.\n  - `crates/app/tests/operations.rs` (`an_entry_edit_marks_the_slot_stale_and_the_orbit_proves_itself`): an orbit is a descending arc. The planar arcs are the lap.\n  - `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_2d_slots.rs`: the Slot now has 8 arc blocks (4 for each level).\n  - `crates/app/tests/clearance_in_stock.rs` (`a_slot_traverse_at_a_clearance_plane_inside_the_stock_is_convicted_and_holds_the_post`): see \"Side effect\" below.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `35020f6cc`: 732 steps, 0 failed.\n- Clippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Side effect (please check in review)\n\nIn `clearance_in_stock`, the slot's lateral traverse between its levels was convicted only because the uncut crescents of the round ends stood in its path. The traverse stays inside the slot's own channel. With the ends cut, the verifier acquits it. The plane is still convicted by the first traverse (`FirstTraverseLow`, #2901) and by the rapid from the plane down into the stock (`RapidInStock { at: 1 }`). The post is still held with \"travels through stock\". The test now asserts these facts.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nAll in `slot_wide_channel_rows` and the catalog case `2d/slots`.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/slot_wide_channel_rows.cl`: 12 lap moves added (2 lines, 10 arcs; each cap split at the rows -7, -3, 1, 5, 7 and the tip). The header changes from `v1` to `v2` because the CL now has arcs.\n- The NC golden of each dialect (`nc/`, `carvera`, `doosan-dnm`, `grbl`, `grblhal`, `haas`, `heidenhain`, `linuxcnc`, `mach4`, `mazak`, `sinumerik`, `tinyg`, `tormach`, `tormach/explain_`): the same 12 moves added. In `heidenhain` and `sinumerik` the block numbers after the lap move up. No other line changes.\n- Catalog case `examples/catalog/2d/slots` (`cargo xtask catalog --case 2d/slots`):\n  - `slots.nc`: 6 lap moves added at each of the two levels (rows at -2, 0, 2: each cap is two quarter arcs).\n  - `slots.camproj`: the cached Slot moves gain the lap. The stamps change.\n  - The first rapid's `from` of the two operations changes from `(0, 0)` to the start point. This change is also in the Trochoidal slot, which this PR does not change. It is drift of the catalog file on main, written by the catalog tool. I kept the tool's output and did not edit it by hand.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) were not run. The change is in `motion` and reaches the `app` heavy lanes. Run them before this PR is flagged ready.\n- The app's `verify` was not run by hand on the catalog case. The suites that post it (`example_catalog`, `solid_law_goldens`) are green.\n- Ramp and Helix entries with the lap ran only through the existing slot tests.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot*.rs` or the catalog case `2d/slots`. The branch merges cleanly with the current `main` (`8be100737`).\n\nChangelog: A Slot wider than its tool now cuts its two round ends to size with a wall lap at each level; before, up to 0.86 mm stayed on the end walls.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2906\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
